From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:23:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/21] drm/msm: wedge the GPU on a failed recovery behind
 msm.wedge_failed_recovery

Our policy so far (default, unchanged): when the hardware init at the end
of ->recover() fails, the queued submits are completed as faulted and
not replayed (fail_queued_submits), and on A8xx a recovery whose CX GDSC
did not collapse completes them too (a8xx_safe_recover). yzddmr6's set
argues that completing hardware fences before a confirmed CX collapse
can let DMA run into freed or reused memory.

With msm.wedge_failed_recovery=1 (read-only, default off) their policy
applies instead:
- A6xx-A8xx share a checked recovery power cycle (a6xx_recover_pm):
  runtime PM and hw_init failures are no longer ignored; a GPU whose
  recovery fails is marked wedged for good: new submits and runtime
  resume get -EIO, the per-ring hangcheck timers stop, queued jobs that
  reach run_job end with -EIO without touching the hardware;
- outstanding hardware fences are completed with -EIO only after a
  confirmed CX power collapse (if hw_init started the CP, the GPU is
  suspended again first); otherwise fences and buffers are kept;
- the fence advance past the hung submit moves after ->recover();
- hardware fences are initialised under gpu->lock only when a submit
  reaches the hardware, so a failure cannot complete future jobs;
- timestamp, debugfs, perf counter and sysprof paths check the runtime
  PM / hw_init result;
- legacy GEM close waits interruptibly and rechecks the wedged state
  once a second, leaving the mappings to the final free, so a process
  can exit while the fences of a wedged GPU stay pending.
Off, every gpu->wedged test is inert (only msm_gpu_recovery_failed(),
reached from the switched paths alone, sets it) and the recover worker,
the A6xx / A8xx recover functions, submit, run_job and the other paths
run the previous code.

Re-implemented from yzddmr6's linux-sm8450-liuqin work (no
Signed-off-by): commit 3700afaa3add ("drm/msm: stop A6xx-A8xx replay when
GPU recovery fails"), itself based on their earlier liuqin change (Link
below), and commit 03dad4b6a375 ("drm/msm: let legacy GEM close exit after
terminal GPU failure"),
adapted to our per-ring hangcheck, hung_ring / recovery_in_progress and
the A8xx safe-recover parameter.

Link: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/018982b5e1ac830617c6aed9cacb6cc68f4eae1a
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
